N:code-refactoring
D:Own behavior-preserving structural improvement. Use when reducing complexity, untangling dependencies, or removing duplication without silently changing semantics.
G:refactoring code-quality maintainability complexity behavior-preservation
U[5]:
  Breaking apart overly mixed responsibilities
  Removing duplication that causes drift
  Creating seams before feature work
  Cleaning up code after a bug fix
  Simplifying structure while preserving behavior
S[5]{n,action}:
  1,Map current behavior and external owners
  2,Choose the required safety net
  3,Pick the smallest structural move
  4,Apply changes incrementally
  5,Verify behavior is still intact
R[4]:
  Default to behavior preservation
  Do not mix refactoring with unrelated feature work
  Do not change contracts without owner approval
  Use testing strategy guidance for the safety net
